1
00:00:11,920 --> 00:00:25,464
大家应该看一下第 6.6 节，内容是对称群；系里的理查德·泰勒教授（Richard Taylor）周五将为我代课，至于作业：他不知道周一要交什么作业，
You should take a look at Section 6.6, which is on the symmetric group; and Richard Taylor, who's a professor in the department, will be subbing for me on Friday. And then the homework:

2
00:00:25,464 --> 00:00:35,657
但周一要交的第 6.6 节作业在这里，然后彼得·克朗海默（Peter Kronheimer）周一讲课，接着理查德讲完的对称群继续往下讲。
he doesn't know the homework due Monday, but here is the homework due Monday in Section 6.6, and then Peter Kronheimer will lecture Monday and pick up where Richard left off on the symmetric group.

3
00:00:35,657 --> 00:00:48,977
所以我想先非常简要地复习一下西罗定理和我们上次给出的证明，然后为大家做几个精彩的应用，让大家看看这些定理是如何使用的。
So I want to just review very briefly the Sylow theorems and their proofs that we did last time, and then do some cool applications for you where you see how you see how these theorems can be used.

4
00:00:48,977 --> 00:01:23,720
请记住这个定理：若 G 是有限群，阶为 n = p^n * m，且 m 与 p 互素，从而 p^n 是整除该群阶数的最高素数幂，那么：(1) 存在阶为 p^n 的西罗 p-子群。
So remember the theorem: if G is finite of order n, which is p^n * m, and m is prime to p, so that p^n is the largest power of a prime dividing the order of the group, then (1) there exist Sylow p-subgroups of order p^n.

5
00:01:23,720 --> 00:02:06,594
所以存在阶为最大素数幂的子群；(2) 任何两个这样的子群都共轭，因此它们构成该阶子群的唯一共轭类；(3) 此类子群的数目 ℓ 满足 ℓ 整除 m，且 ℓ ≡ 1 mod p。那么一个总是能满足此条件的典型数值就是 ℓ = 1。
So there are subgroups of the maximum power prime order; (2) any two such subgroups are conjugate, so they form a unique conjugacy class of subgroups of that order; and (3) the number \ell of such subgroups satisfies \ell divides m, and \ell is congruent to 1 mod p. So a typical number that can always satisfy this is \ell = 1.

6
00:02:06,594 --> 00:02:22,687
西罗子群总是可能是正规的，且只有一个，可能 ℓ = 1，即西罗子群是 G 的正规子群。
It's always possible that the Sylow subgroups are normal, and there's only one, possible that \ell = 1, i.e., that the Sylow subgroup is a normal subgroup of G.

7
00:02:22,687 --> 00:02:36,480
这当然是可能的，虽然并非总是如此，但这是可能发生的——任何两个这样的子群都会共轭，即只有唯一一个，因此那将是唯一的西罗 p-子群。
That's certainly possible, doesn't always happen, but that's something that could—any two such would be conjugate, there would namely be only one of them, so that would be a unique Sylow p-subgroup.

8
00:02:38,590 --> 00:02:44,240
当然也可能有更多个，但在任何情况下根据第 (2) 条，它们全都彼此共轭。
And then, but there could be more; but in any case, under (2), they're all conjugate.

9
00:02:44,240 --> 00:03:11,136
这就是西罗定理的内容。有问题吗？没有，只是伸懒腰？大家看，如果……一个整除 m 且同余于1 mod p 的数就是 1，即 ℓ = 1。大家总可以先尝试 ℓ = 1。
So that's the content of the Sylow theorems. Yes? No questions, a stretch? You see, if there's... one number \ell that divides m and is congruent to 1 mod p is 1, \ell = 1. You can always try \ell = 1.

10
00:03:11,136 --> 00:03:27,052
可能还有其他数满足条件，但总有这种可能——如果只有一个西罗子群，那么由第 (2) 条可知它必为正规子群，因为 H 的任何共轭仍是西罗子群。
There may be other numbers that satisfy this, but there's always possibility that one—if there's only one Sylow subgroup, then by number (2), it says that it must be normal, because any conjugate of H would be a Sylow subgroup.

11
00:03:27,052 --> 00:03:45,811
我是说，如果你有一个 p^n 阶子群，若 H 的阶为 p^n，那么它的共轭 H' = g H g^{-1} 也具有阶 p^n，即 H 的共轭。
I mean, if you had a subgroup of order p^n, so if H has order p^n, so does H' which is g H g^{-1}, a conjugate of H.

12
00:03:45,811 --> 00:04:15,244
如果只有唯一一个西罗子群，那么这些共轭全部等于 H，因为无论它是谁，它都是西罗 p-子群，阶相同，所以 H 在 G 中正规。反之，若 H 在 G 中正规，则只有唯一一个西罗p-子群。
If there's only one Sylow subgroup, then these are all equal to H, because whatever this is, it's a Sylow p-subgroup, it has the same order, and therefore H is normal in G. Conversely, if H is normal in G, there is only one Sylow p-subgroup.

13
00:04:15,244 --> 00:04:31,749
原因是任何两个西罗子群都共轭，所以如果有另一个，你就能把 H 共轭成 H'；但说 H 在 G 中正规意味着 H 的所有共轭都等于 H。明白这个想法了吗？这很值得牢牢记在脑子里。
The reason is that any two of them are conjugate, so if you had another one, you'd be able to conjugate H into H', but saying that H is normal in G means that all conjugates of H are equal to H. Got that idea now? Good thing to fix in your mind.

14
00:04:31,749 --> 00:04:48,933
好，让我们非常快速地回顾一下证明。我带大家过一遍：核心全在于群在集合上的作用，通过群作用于集合。
All right, let's recall the proof very, very quickly. I'm going to walk you through it: it's all about groups acting on sets, via groups acting on sets.

15
00:04:48,933 --> 00:05:23,108
关键原理是：如果 G……好，首先要做的是让 G 通过左平移作用在 G 的大小为 p^n 的子集构成的集合 S 上。将 g 作用在子集上定义为子集 g * J。
And the key principle is: if G... All right, so the first thing you do is you have G act by translation on the set—I don't know, S—of subsets J in G where the size of J is p^n. So you take g of a subset is the subset g * J.

16
00:05:23,108 --> 00:05:39,046
这就是我说的平移。它置换大小为 p^n 的子集，因为如果 J 的大小为 p^n，那么与 g 的乘积也具有大小 p^n。
That's what I mean by translation. So it permutes around the subsets of size p^n, because if this has size p^n, then all products with g have size p^n.

17
00:05:39,046 --> 00:05:48,770
这类子集的总数等于组合数 C(n, p^n)，我们此前证明了它与 p 互素。
The number of such subsets is equal to \binom{n}{p^n}, which we showed is prime to p.

18
00:05:50,730 --> 00:06:02,389
所以某个轨道 𝒪 的大小与 p 互素。
So some orbit \mathcal{O} of J has size prime to p.

19
00:06:03,739 --> 00:06:24,979
从而该子集的稳定子群的阶能被 p^n 整除，因为轨道的大小等于 G 的阶除以稳定子群的阶。
So the stabilizer of that subset has order divisible by p^n, because the size of the orbit is the order of G divided by the order of the stabilizer.

20
00:06:24,979 --> 00:06:40,083
但任何子集的稳定子群的大小都小于或等于 p^n，小于或等于 p^n。
But the stabilizer of any subset has size less than or equal to p^n, less than or equal to p^n.

21
00:06:40,083 --> 00:07:01,234
上次我稍微略过了一点，这是出于下面这个显而易见的原因：若 j 属于子集 J 且 g ∈ G_J，则 g j 属于该子集，对吧？
And I sort of fudged a little bit, and this is for the following obvious reason: if j is in the subset and g is in G_J, then g j is in the subset, all right?

22
00:07:01,234 --> 00:07:20,060
我是说，这就是属于该子集稳定子群的含义：若左乘在 j 上，结果仍落在子集内。这在 J 中给出了 |G_J| 个元素，对吧？
I mean, that's what it means to be in the stabilizer of this subset: if you act by the left on j, you stay inside the subset. All right, this gives the order of G_J elements in J, right?

23
00:07:20,060 --> 00:07:24,917
因此这个数目必须小于或等于 J 中的元素数。
Therefore this number has to be less than the number of things in J.

24
00:07:24,917 --> 00:07:43,146
所以 G_J 中的元素数必须小于或等于 J 的大小。于是我们得到了一个子群，其阶可被 p^n 整除，且阶小于或等于 p^n。
So the number of things in G_J has to be less than or equal to the size of J. So then I have a subgroup which has order divisible by p^n, which has order less than or equal to p^n.

25
00:07:43,146 --> 00:07:54,339
这推导出 G_J 的阶恰好是 p^n，是一个西罗 p-子群。这就是第 (1) 部分的证明。
That implies that G_J has order p^n, and is a Sylow p-subgroup. And that was the proof of (1).

26
00:07:57,050 --> 00:08:13,158
这黑板擦怎么了？它就在真黑板擦旁边。真的黑板擦在哪……在这呢，抱歉。一旦有了西罗 p-子群，我们就可以开始做轨道分析了。
What is this going over here? It's just near my real eraser. Where is the real... here's the real eraser, I'm sorry. Once we have a Sylow p-subgroup, then we start doing orbit questions.

27
00:08:13,158 --> 00:08:17,981
所以在第二部分 (2) 中，我们改变所作用的集合。
So the next part, (2), we change our set that we're acting on.

28
00:08:17,981 --> 00:08:56,639
设 H 为西罗 p-子群，让 G 通过左平移传递地作用在 H 的陪集空间上，该陪集空间的阶为 m（与 p 互素）。我们再次构造出一个阶与 p 互素的集合。
You now have: let H be a Sylow p-subgroup, and let G act by translation transitively on the coset space of H, which has order m prime to p. Again, we construct the set of order prime to p.

29
00:08:56,639 --> 00:09:15,175
但现在既然已证明了第 (1) 部分，拥有了一个阶为 p^n 的子群 H，我们就可以将群所作用的集合换成这个。通过平移，群在上面传递地作用，因为群在陪集空间上的平移总是传递的。
But now, since we've proved (1), so that we have a subgroup, call it H, of order p^n, we can change our set that the group is acting on to be this. By translation, it acts transitively on it, because it always acts transitively on a coset space.

30
00:09:15,175 --> 00:09:37,891
于是陪集 g H 的稳定子群是西罗 p-子群 g H g^{-1}，因为陪集 H 的稳定子群……我们从一般作用中已知这点。
So the stabilizer of the coset g H is the Sylow p-subgroup g H g^{-1}, because the stabilizer of the coset H... We know this from our general action,

31
00:09:37,891 --> 00:10:06,888
我们只需证明任何西罗 p-子群都具有这种形式。所以只需证明：设 H' 为任意西罗 p-子群，将G 在 G/H 上的作用限制到 H' 上。
and we have to show that any Sylow p-subgroup is of this form. So it suffices to show: let H' be a Sylow p-subgroup, and restrict the G-action on G/H to H'.

32
00:10:07,270 --> 00:10:16,440
那我断言这是一个阶与 p 互素的集合，而 H' 是一个阶为p 的幂的群，对吧？
Well, I claim this is a set of order prime to p, this is a group of order a power of p, right?

33
00:10:16,440 --> 00:10:18,862
因此它必须固定某个点！
Therefore it has to fix something!

34
00:10:18,862 --> 00:10:49,695
因为如果它不固定任何点，轨道的阶就全都能被 p 整除：轨道的大小为 p^a，其中 0 ≤ a ≤ n，因为 H' 的轨道大小形式为：H' 的阶除以稳定子群的阶，而稳定子群是 H' 的子群，所以这必是 p 的幂。
Because if it didn't fix something, the orbits would all have size divisible by p: the orbits have size p^a for 0 <= a <= n, because the orbits for H' are of the form: the order of H' divided by the stabilizer, and the stabilizer is a subgroup of H', so this is a power of p.

35
00:10:49,695 --> 00:11:09,167
如果所有轨道的大小都能被 p 整除，那么所有轨道大小的总和也必能被 p 整除，但事实并非如此，因为所作用的整个空间的阶与 p 互素。
If all of these were divisible by p, then the sum of the size of the orbits would also be divisible by p, which it isn't, because this total space that they're acting on has order prime to p.

36
00:11:09,167 --> 00:11:27,660
因此必有某个轨道的大小为 1（不能被 p 整除）；既然大小为 1，这意味着 H' 固定了该点，这意味着 H' 包含在该点的稳定子群中。
So some orbit has size 1, not divisible by p; and since it has size 1, that means that H' fixes the point, which means that H' is contained in this stabilizer of the point.

37
00:11:31,280 --> 00:11:36,249
但这两个群具有相同的阶，所以 H' 恰好等于该稳定子群。
But these groups have the same order, so H' is equal to that stabilizer.

38
00:11:36,249 --> 00:11:54,509
这就是第 (2) 部分的证明。而第 (3) 部分的证明是另一个群作用在另一个与 p 互素的集合上。让我们重温第 (3) 部分，因为在某种意义上最巧妙。
So that's the proof of (2). And the proof of (3) is another group action on another set prime to p. So let's go through (3) again, because that's in some sense the most clever.

39
00:11:54,509 --> 00:12:11,745
每一个都利用前面的结论来构造一个不同的群作用：第一个我们只知道群的阶是这个，然后构造了在子集上的作用；一旦有了西罗 p-子群，我们就有这个集合可供作用；现在既然知道它们全部共轭，
Each one uses the previous to construct a different group action: the first one we just knew that the order of the group was this, and we constructed an action on subsets. Once we had Sylow p-subgroups, we had this set to act on. Now that we know they're all conjugate,

40
00:12:11,745 --> 00:12:53,605
(3) 既然所有西罗子群都共轭，我们就有 G 通过共轭——不是平移——传递地作用在所有西罗子群构成的集合 ℋ 上。这就是我们试图计算基数的集合，对吧？这个集合。
(3) since all Sylows are conjugate, we have the transitive action of G by conjugation—not by translation—on the set \mathcal{H} of all Sylows. This is the set that we're trying to count, right? This set.

41
00:12:53,605 --> 00:13:15,367
对于这个作用，H 的稳定子群就是群 G_H，即我们称为 H 的正规化子的群 N_G(H)，因此集合 ℋ（无论具体是什么）都可以等同于 G 模去 H 的正规化子 G/N_G(H)，是一个陪集空间，因为这是传递作用，对吧？
The stabilizer of H for this action is the group G_H that we call the normalizer of H, so therefore the set \mathcal{H}, whatever it is, is identified with G modulo the normalizer of H, is a coset space, because it's a transitive action, right?

42
00:13:15,367 --> 00:13:42,243
所以无论它是什么，它的阶都整除 m：H 的正规化子包含 H，所以这个商集的阶整除 m，因为 H 的指数是 m，所以正规化子的指数无论是什么，都是 m 的因子，对吧？明白了吗？
So whatever this is, the order of this divides m: normalizer of H contains H, so the order of this quotient set divides m, because the index of H is m, so whatever the index of the normalizer is, it's a divisor of m, right? Got that?

43
00:13:42,243 --> 00:13:58,296
H 的正规化子介于 H与 G 之间，总指数是 m，所以这个指数无论是多少都是 m 的因子。这个指数乘以那个指数就是总指数，好的，整除 m。
Normalizer of H is between this and G, this total number is m, so whatever this index is, is a divisor of m. This index times this index is the whole index, okay, divides m.

44
00:13:58,296 --> 00:14:55,070
这是定理第 (3) 部分的前半截。后半截是：我们考虑 H 在此集合上的作用。现在考虑H 通过共轭在 ℋ 上的作用。G 传递地置换它们，但 H 则不然。例如，H 将自身共轭到自身，所以它固定了 H。而我断言这是唯一的不动点！
That's the first part of the theorem. The second part is: we consider the action of H on this set. Now consider the action of H by conjugation on \mathcal{H}. Now G permutes them transitively, but H doesn't. For example, H conjugates itself into itself, so this fixes H. And I claim this is the unique fixed point!

45
00:14:55,484 --> 00:15:05,030
因此所有其他轨道的大小都能被 p 整除，因为轨道大小等于 H 的阶除以稳定子群的阶，而这是一个 p-群。
So all other orbits have size divisible by p, because the orbit is the order of H divided by the stabilizer subgroup, which is a p-group.

46
00:15:05,030 --> 00:15:21,918
如果所有其他轨道的大小都能被 p 整除，且存在唯一不动点，那么该集合中的元素总数就同余于 1 mod p，因为可以写成能被 p 整除的各项之和加上 1。所以我只需向大家证明：这是该作用在集合上的唯一不动点。
And if all the other orbits have size divisible by p, and there's a unique fixed point, then the number of elements in this set is congruent to 1 mod p, because the sum of things divisible by p plus 1. So all I have to show you is that this is a unique fixed point for the action.

47
00:15:21,918 --> 00:15:42,603
好，假设存在另一个不动点：那意味着如果 H' 在 H 的共轭作用下固定，那么 H 和 H'都包含在 H' 的正规化子中，
Well, suppose there was another fixed point: that would say if H' is fixed by conjugation by H, then both H and H' are contained in the normalizer of H',

48
00:15:42,603 --> 00:15:54,093
因为说 H 在共轭下固定 H'，意味着 H 是H' 的正规化子的子群，而正规化子恰好就是在 G 的共轭下固定 H' 的全体元素。
because to say that H fixes H' under conjugation means that H is a subgroup of the normalizer of H', which is exactly what fixes H' when you conjugate by G.

49
00:15:54,093 --> 00:16:15,477
好，问题在于它们都是 H' 的正规化子的西罗 p-子群，因为该正规化子的阶无论是什么，都是 p^n * m' 的形式，而这两个群的阶都是 p^n。
Okay, the problem with that is that they're both Sylow p-subgroups of the normalizer of H', because whatever the order of this is, it's some p^n * m', and these both have order p^n.

50
00:16:15,477 --> 00:16:19,715
所以它们都是这个新群（即 G 的该子群）里的西罗子群。
So they're both Sylows in a new group, namely in that group which is a subgroup of G.

51
00:16:19,715 --> 00:16:31,329
但我们在第 (2) 部分证明过，对任何有限群，任意两个西罗子群都共轭。因此，它们必须在 H' 的正规化子中也是共轭的。
But we proved in part (2) that for any finite group, any two Sylow subgroups are conjugate. Therefore they have to be conjugate in the normalizer of H'.

52
00:16:31,329 --> 00:16:44,540
但是 H' 的正规化子包含 H'作为正规子群；请记住，当子群正规时，它就是唯一的西罗 p-子群！因此 H 必须等于 H'。
But the normalizer of H' contains H' as a normal subgroup, and remember, when we had a normal subgroup, it was the unique Sylow p-subgroup! Therefore H has to be equal to H'.

53
00:16:44,540 --> 00:17:08,412
所以这个我们原以为是不同不动点的不动点，实际上就等于 H。两者都是西罗子群，H' 在其正规化子中正规，因而就是唯一的西罗子群，所以 H = H'。
And therefore this fixed point that we thought was a distinct fixed point is actually equal to H. Both Sylows, H' is normal in the normalizer of H', so is the unique Sylow, so H is equal to H'.

54
00:17:08,412 --> 00:17:15,405
因此这就完成了该数目同余于 1 mod p 的最终证明：在作用中存在唯一不动点。
And therefore that's the final proof that the number is congruent to 1 mod p: there's a unique fixed point in the action.

55
00:17:15,405 --> 00:17:33,780
如果取 G 在所有西罗 p-子群上的共轭作用，它是传递的；如果限制到 H，任何西罗 p-子群，它都有唯一不动点——即它自身，在共轭下不固定任何其他西罗子群。所以这是……这是太棒了，这真是一流的数学！
If you take the action of G by conjugation on the Sylow p-subgroups, it acts transitively; if you restrict that to H, any Sylow p-subgroup, it has a unique fixed point, its own Sylow p-subgroup, doesn't fix any of the others by conjugation. So this is... this is great, this is just great mathematics!

56
00:17:33,780 --> 00:17:43,529
还能说什么呢？真希望当年是我想出来的！这绝对是有限群分类中最核心的结论。
What can you say? I wish I had thought of it! And it's absolutely a central result in the classification of finite groups.

57
00:17:43,529 --> 00:17:53,931
正如我所说，有一个庞大的工程——我真该把那本《有限单群图集》（Atlas of Finite Groups）带过来的——20 世纪后期的宏伟工程：分类所有有限单群。
As I said, there's a huge project—I should have brought in my book on the *Atlas of Finite Groups*—the huge project in the late 20th century to classify all finite simple groups.

58
00:17:53,931 --> 00:18:07,586
起点永远是西罗定理，永远是西罗定理！因为对于任何有限群，它能立即为你提供一整套子群，你不仅知道它们全都是共轭的，还大致知道有多少个，至少有某种估计，然后可以尝试由这些子群拼装出整个群。
The start is always the Sylow theorems, always the Sylow theorems! Because it gives you immediately, for any finite group, a large host of subgroups where you know they're all conjugate, you know about how many of them there are, at least you have some estimate on it, and you can try to build the group out of those subgroups.

59
00:18:07,586 --> 00:18:47,649
所以我今天要做的是，向大家展示这如何影响小阶数群的分类，从而让大家对西罗定理在实际中如何用于刻画所有 6 阶群、所有 15 阶群或所有 21 阶群有些直观感受。请记住我们目前已有的结论：分类定理。
So what I'm going to do for you today is I'm going to show how this affects the classification of groups of small order, so you can get some idea of how Sylow's theorem can be used in action to describe all the groups of order 6, or all the groups of order 15, or all the groups of order 21. So remember what we've got so far: we know the classification theorems.

60
00:18:47,649 --> 00:18:59,326
我们已经证明：若 G 的阶为素数 p，则 G 是循环群，同构于 Z/pZ。
We've shown: if the order of G is p, a prime, then G is cyclic and isomorphic to Z/pZ.

61
00:18:59,326 --> 00:19:31,296
若 G 的阶为 p^2，则 G 是交换群，且有两种可能：若没有 p^2 阶元素，则同构于 (Z/pZ)^2；或者同构于循环群Z/p^2Z：前者是所有 g ≠ e 均满足 g^p = e，后者是存在某个阶不是p 的元素。
If the order of G is p^2, then G is abelian, and there are two possibilities: it could either be isomorphic to (Z/pZ)^2 if there were no element of order p^2, or it could be isomorphic to the cyclic group Z/p^2Z: this is all g \ne e satisfy g^p = e, and this is there is some element which doesn't have order p.

62
00:19:31,296 --> 00:19:42,986
好，现在我们来处理 pq，两个素数，我们假设 p < q。其中一个必须小于另一个。
All right, now we're going to do pq, two primes, and we'll assume that p is less than q. One of them has to be less than the other.

63
00:19:42,986 --> 00:19:55,220
好，在我们代入具体的 p 和 q 之前，先来做几点观察。是的，为什么不呢？这样我们就能着手进行了。
All right, let's make some observations about this before we do actual p's and q's. Yeah, why not? So that we can get started.

64
00:19:55,220 --> 00:20:15,309
第一点是：存在子群 H_p、H_q，分别为 p 阶和 q 阶西罗子群。
The first is: there exist subgroups H_p, H_q, Sylow subgroups of order p and q.

65
00:20:15,309 --> 00:20:25,219
由西罗定理，这些因子能产生子群，因为我们将群的阶写成 p * q，且 p 与 q 互素，所以可以应用两次定理，对。
Those divisors give rise to subgroups by the Sylow theorems, because we write the order of the group as p * q, and p is prime to q, so I apply it twice, yeah.

66
00:20:25,219 --> 00:20:39,640
q 是素数，两者都是素数，抱歉，否则我们就不会知道存在 q 阶子群。所以就像 6、15 或 21。
q is prime, yeah, they're both prime, I'm sorry, otherwise we wouldn't know there was a subgroup of order q. So it's like 6, or 15, or 21.

67
00:20:39,640 --> 00:21:00,980
好，第二点是：作为集合，G 等于 H_p 与 H_q 中元素的乘积。这两个群都是循环群，分别同构于 Z/pZ 和 Z/qZ。
Okay, second thing is that as a set, G is equal to the product of elements in H_p and H_q. Both of these are cyclic, isomorphic to Z/pZ and Z/qZ.

68
00:21:00,980 --> 00:21:09,229
这来自我们之前的分类，因为它们的阶是素数。所以无论那些子群是什么，我们都知道它们的结构：它们是循环群。
That's from our previous classification, because they have prime order. So whatever those subgroups are, we know what they are: they're cyclic groups.

69
00:21:09,229 --> 00:21:13,465
其次，作为集合，G 是 H_p 与 H_q 中元素的乘积。
Secondly, as a set, G is the product of elements in H_p and H_q.

70
00:21:13,465 --> 00:21:38,309
所以它是这种形式：设这个 p 阶循环子群由 τ 生成，而这个 q 阶循环子群由 σ 生成，那么元素就形如 τ^a σ^b，满足0 ≤ a < p 且 0 ≤ b < q。
So it's something of the form: let's say this cyclic subgroup of order p is generated by \tau, and this cyclic subgroup of order q is generated by \sigma, so this would be of the form \tau^a \sigma^b, such that 0 <= a < p and 0 <= b < q.

71
00:21:38,309 --> 00:21:59,570
因为 H_q 的元素是 σ 在 0 到 q 之间的各次幂，H_p 的元素是 τ 在 0 到 p 之间的各次幂；而且我断言，如果取遍 H_p 中的所有元素并乘以 H_q 中的元素，就能得到整个群。好的，为什么呢？
Because the elements of H_q are the powers of \sigma between 0 and q, the elements of H_p are the powers of \tau between 0 and p; and I claim that if you take all elements in H_p and multiply by elements in H_q, you get the entire group. Okay, why?

72
00:21:59,570 --> 00:22:08,030
这其实就是说H_p 中的元素代表了 H_q 的各个不同的左陪集。
Well, this is just saying that the elements in H_p represent the distinct left cosets of H_q.

73
00:22:08,030 --> 00:22:24,075
即 G 等于各个不同 τ 的陪集 τ^a H_q 的并集，即对 0 ≤ a < p。
Namely, that G is equal to the union of (\tau^a H_q) for the different \tau's, or you know, yeah, for 0 <= a < p.

74
00:22:24,075 --> 00:22:36,677
那么，只需证明这些陪集互不相同即可，对吧？因为每个陪集含有 q 个元素，且对应 p 个不同的H_p 元素共有 p 个陪集。
Well, it's enough to prove that these sets are distinct, right? Because each coset has q elements in it, and there are p cosets for the p different elements in H_p.

75
00:22:36,677 --> 00:22:51,957
因此只要能证明这些陪集两两不交，它们就必然构成整个群。
So as long as we can prove that these cosets are distinct, they have to give us the whole group.

76
00:22:51,957 --> 00:23:11,970
而它们对 H_p 中不同的 τ 和 τ' 是两两不相交的，因为若有等式 τ H_q = τ' H_q，就会推导出 τ (τ')^{-1}是 H_q 中的元素，对吧？
And they're distinct for distinct \tau and \tau' in H_p, because if we had an equality \tau H_q = \tau' H_q, that would imply that \tau \tau'^{-1} was an element in H_q, right?

77
00:23:11,970 --> 00:23:22,323
进而推导出元素 τ (τ')^{-1} 属于 H_p 与 H_q 的交集。
Which would imply that this element \tau \tau'^{-1} was in the intersection of H_p and H_q.

78
00:23:22,323 --> 00:23:30,313
而H_p 与 H_q 的交集是两者的公共子群，所以其阶既整除 p，又整除 q。
And the intersection of H_p and H_q is a subgroup of both of them, so has order dividing p, but also has order dividing q.

79
00:23:30,313 --> 00:23:36,517
而同时整除 p 和 q 的数只有 1，因此这两个群的交集只有单位元。
And the only number that divides both p and q is 1, so the intersection of these two groups is the identity.

80
00:23:36,517 --> 00:23:44,656
所以如果这两个陪集相等，该元素就必须是单位元；换句话说，H_p 中的元素必须相等。
So if we have the equality of these two cosets, this element has to be the identity; in other words, we have to have the equality of elements in H_p.

81
00:23:44,656 --> 00:23:58,391
所以仅仅依靠西罗定理，我们就已知群是由这两个循环子群构成的；而我们唯一真正需要弄清楚的，就是如何将这里的两个元素相乘，对吧？
So we already know, just from the Sylow theorems, that our group is made out of these two cyclic subgroups; and the only thing we really have to figure out is how to multiply two things here, right?

82
00:23:58,391 --> 00:24:12,726
特别地，我们想知道：当你试图计算乘积 (τ^a σ^b)(τ^{a'} σ^{b'})等于什么时，若想写成标准形式，就必须将其化为 τ 的幂次乘以 σ 的幂次。
And in particular, we'd like this: when you're trying to multiply (\tau^a \sigma^b) * (\tau^{a'} \sigma^{b'}) is equal to what?

83
00:24:12,726 --> 00:24:28,125
而基本上，你必须弄清楚如何对调这两个元素，对吧？当把 σ 与 τ 相乘，试图将其换为 τ 乘以σ 时会发生什么？
You have to write it as a power of \tau times a power of \sigma, if you want to write it in this form. And basically, you have to figure out how to commute these two elements across, right? What happens when you multiply \sigma by \tau, and you try to turn it into a \tau by \sigma?

84
00:24:28,125 --> 00:24:39,350
好，这就是确定 pq 阶群结构的全部核心问题：当你试图相乘时，这两个生成元如何穿过彼此？所以我来为大家推导。
Okay, so that's the whole problem of determining the structure of groups of order pq: how do these two generators cross each other when you try to multiply them?

85
00:24:39,350 --> 00:25:23,018
好的，我想做出的第一个观察（这看起来有点奇妙），是的，第一个观察是：H_q 永远是 G 的正规子群。这是完全普适的：H_p 可能不正规，但 H_q 永远正规，即较大素数对应的子群必正规。
So I'm going to work that out for you. Okay, so the first observation I want to make, which is kind of bizarre, yeah, the first observation I want to make is that this H_q is always a normal subgroup of G. This is completely general: H_p may not be normal, but H_q is always normal, the bigger prime.

86
00:25:23,018 --> 00:25:38,861
原因是：西罗 q-子群的数目 ℓ 整除 p 且 ℓ ≡ 1 mod q。
And the reason is this: the number of Sylow q-subgroups, \ell, divides p and is congruent to 1 mod q.

87
00:25:38,861 --> 00:26:00,725
那么，任何不为 1 且模 q 同余于 1 的数都至少是 q + 1，但 p < q，所以它绝不可能整除 p，对吧？
Well, any number other than 1 which is congruent to 1 mod q is at least q + 1, but p is less than q, so it couldn't divide p, right?

88
00:26:00,725 --> 00:26:06,024
所以唯一的可能就是 ℓ = 1，唯一的可能，因为 q 大于 p！
So the only such possibility is \ell = 1, the only possibility, because q is bigger than p!

89
00:26:06,024 --> 00:26:29,040
因此它正规这一事实意味着：如果取 τσ τ^{-1}，它必须是 σ 的某次幂，因为无论该元素是什么，它都落在 H_q 中。
So the fact that it's normal means the following: that if I take \tau \sigma \tau^{-1}, that has to be a power of \sigma, because whatever this element is, it's in H_q.

90
00:26:32,190 --> 00:26:43,910
而群的全部结构……所以这说明 τ σ = σ^a τ，而群的全部结构只取决于这个指数 a 是多少，仅仅取决于它。
And the whole structure of the group is that... So this says that \tau \sigma = \sigma^a \tau, and the whole structure of the group depends on what this a is, that's all it depends on.

91
00:26:43,910 --> 00:26:57,090
因为一旦知道 a 是什么，我就能知道如何让两者对调穿过。所以这个神秘的数 a 决定了群，我们必须弄清楚：a 有哪些可能的取值？
Because once I know what a is, I can figure out how to commute these two across. So this mysterious number a determines the group, and we have to figure out: what are the possibilities for a?

92
00:26:57,090 --> 00:27:04,250
现在我们来代入几个具体的 p 和 q，大家就能体会到了。
Now we're going to do some specific p and q, and you'll get the feeling for it.

93
00:27:04,250 --> 00:27:19,141
我这里稍微略过了一点细节，我是说，如我所言，大家现在必须明白一旦知道了这个数，就可以将这种形式与那种形式相乘，并化为 τ 的幂乘 σ 的幂。
So I'm fudging a little here, I mean, as I say, you now have to see that once you know what this number is, you can multiply something like this, something like that, and turn it into a power of \tau times a power of \sigma.

94
00:27:19,141 --> 00:27:33,937
大家必须相信我这一点，你们私下自己算一下就行，并不难。我们先试试 6 阶群，然后做 p * q = 15 的情形。
You have to believe me on that, you'll just do that, you know, quietly yourself, it's not hard. Let's try groups of order 6, then we'll do p * q = 15.

95
00:27:33,937 --> 00:27:45,060
好，这里 H_q 是3 阶的，形式如下：{1, σ, σ^2}。H_p 是 2 阶的：{1, τ}。
Okay, so here H_q is of order 3, it looks like this: {1, \sigma, \sigma^2}. H_p is of order 2: {1, \tau}.

96
00:27:45,060 --> 00:27:57,815
好，我们必须弄清楚：τ σ τ^{-1} 有哪些可能？它可以是 σ，这毫无问题！
Okay, we have to figure out: what's the possibility for \tau \sigma \tau^{-1}? Well, it could be \sigma, no problem there!

97
00:27:57,815 --> 00:28:26,019
那只是说 τ 与 σ 对易，那么该群就是交换群，因为它由 τ 和 σ 生成：若它们对易，一切都对易，τ σ = σ τ，G 是交换群，而且事实上你会发现它同构于 Z/6Z，由 στ 生成。
That would just say that \tau commuted with \sigma, then the group would be abelian, because it's generated by \tau and \sigma: if they commute, everything commutes, \tau \sigma = \sigma \tau, G is abelian, and in fact, you'll find it's isomorphic to Z/6Z, generated by \sigma \tau.

98
00:28:26,019 --> 00:28:46,667
即 σ 具有 3 阶，τ 具有 2 阶，因为它们对易，你可以证明στ 的阶为 6；而在 6 阶群中若有 6 阶元素，它就是循环群。所以如果这个元素是 σ，我们就得到了一个交换群。
Namely, \sigma has order 3, \tau has order 2, since they commute you can prove that this has order 6; and if you have an element of order 6 in a group of order 6, it's cyclic. So if this element was \sigma, we get an abelian group.

99
00:28:46,667 --> 00:28:55,921
还有什么其他可能？它必须是 σ 的某次幂。它不能是 1：你不可能把一个非平凡元素共轭成单位元。
What are the other possibilities? Well, it's got to be some power of \sigma. It can't be 1: you can't conjugate a non-trivial element into the identity.

100
00:28:55,921 --> 00:29:08,230
所以唯一的另一种可能是：它能否是 σ^2？答案是可以，这与 σ^{-1} 相同，因为这是 3 阶群。
So the only other possibility is: could it be \sigma^2? The answer is yeah, that's the same as \sigma^{-1}, because this is a group of order 3.

101
00:29:08,230 --> 00:29:16,900
而我们早就知道一个包含 3 阶循环子群、且有一个 2 阶元素将该3 阶元素共轭为其逆元的群。
And we already know a group that has a cyclic subgroup of order 3, an element of order 2 that conjugates that element of order 3 into its inverse.

102
00:29:16,900 --> 00:29:20,160
那叫什么群？对称群！
What's that called? The symmetric group!

103
00:29:20,160 --> 00:29:30,108
更一般地，是二面体群：记住，二面体群包含一个n 阶循环子群，以及一个将该元素共轭为其逆元的 2 阶元素。就是这样！
More generally, it's the dihedral group: the dihedral group, remember, contains a cyclic subgroup of order n, an element of order 2 that conjugates the element into its inverse. So here it is!

104
00:29:30,108 --> 00:29:41,092
所以 G 同构于6 阶二面体群，在本例中它也是 3 个字母上的对称群 S_3。
So G is isomorphic to the dihedral group of order 6, also in this case it's the symmetric group on three letters S_3.

105
00:29:41,092 --> 00:29:57,871
所以通过这个利用西罗定理的论证，我们不仅得到了 2 阶和 3 阶子群，还证明了 3 阶子群必须正规，因此当你对它共轭时，必须得到 σ 的某次幂；这正好向我们证明了 6 阶群只有两种。
So here we've just shown, by this argument using the Sylow theorems that gave us not only the subgroups of order 2 and 3, but proved that the subgroup of order 3 has to be normal, and so when you conjugate it you have to get some power of \sigma, it just proves to us that there are only two groups of order 6.

106
00:29:57,871 --> 00:30:10,096
如果得到 σ 的1 次幂，就得到 6 阶循环交换群；如果得到 2 次幂 σ^2，就得到 6 阶二面体群，或 3 个字母上的对称群。
If you get the first power of \sigma, you got an abelian group which is cyclic of order 6; and if you get the second power, \sigma^2, you get the dihedral group of order 6, or the symmetric group on three letters.

107
00:30:10,096 --> 00:30:16,400
好，现在你可能会说：“通常情况大概也是这样吧”，那你就错了！
Okay, now you might say, "Well, that's probably what happens in general," and you'd be wrong!

108
00:30:18,180 --> 00:30:33,878
但实际上，我们何不先做阶为 2q 的一般情形呢？因为这样你就会看到完全相同的事情发生。
But in fact, why don't we do the general case of 2q, order of G? Because then you'll see that the exact same thing happens.

109
00:30:33,878 --> 00:30:48,490
也就是说，在此情形下 H_q 是 {1, σ, σ^2, ..., σ^{q-1}}，其中最后这一项就是 σ^{-1}；H_2 只有 {1, τ}，对吧？
Namely, in this case H_q is {1, \sigma, \sigma^2, ..., \sigma^{q-1}}, which is the same as \sigma^{-1}; H_2 is just {1, \tau}, right?

110
00:30:48,490 --> 00:31:10,478
我们再次发现 τ σ τ^{-1} 是 σ 的某次幂，而我断言这个 a 必为 ±1，所以只有两种可能。
And again we find that \tau \sigma \tau^{-1} is some power of \sigma, and I claim that this a is plus or minus 1, so there are only two possibilities.

111
00:31:10,478 --> 00:31:19,781
确切地说，它在模 q 下同余于 ±1，因为如果考虑这些幂次，关键只在于幂次模 q 的值。
Well, it's really congruent to plus or minus 1 mod q, because if you think of these powers, it only matters what the power is mod q.

112
00:31:19,781 --> 00:31:32,400
q - 1 模 q 同余于 -1，这就等同于 σ^{-1}，因为 σ^q 是单位元。原因是：将此操作复合两次！
If q - 1 is congruent to -1 mod q, this would be the same as \sigma^{-1}, because \sigma^q is the identity. And the reason is: do this twice!

113
00:31:32,400 --> 00:31:47,940
如果 τ σ τ^{-1} = σ^a，那么 τ^2 σ τ^{-2} 是什么呢？一方面，它是τ (τ σ τ^{-1}) τ^{-1}。
If \tau \sigma \tau^{-1} = \sigma^a, then what about \tau^2 \sigma \tau^{-2}? Well, on the one hand, that is \tau (\tau \sigma \tau^{-1}) \tau^{-1}.

114
00:31:47,940 --> 00:32:14,719
括号里是 σ^a，所以是 τ (σ^a) τ^{-1}，这等价于……把它写成 σ^a 乘 σ^a 乘 σ^a……乘 σ^a，一共a 次！
This is supposed to be \sigma^a, so it's \tau (\sigma^a) \tau^{-1}, which is the same thing as applying... well, it's \sigma^a * \sigma^a * \sigma^a * ... * \sigma^a, a times!

115
00:32:14,719 --> 00:32:25,489
因为你把它拆成 (τ σ τ^{-1}) * (τ σ τ^{-1}) * (τ σ τ^{-1})，共 a 次，对吧？
Because you break this up into (\tau \sigma \tau^{-1}) * (\tau \sigma \tau^{-1}) * (\tau \sigma \tau^{-1}), a times, right?

116
00:32:25,489 --> 00:32:43,322
这就会给出这个式子，因为中间的 τ 和 τ^{-1} 全部相互抵消了，然后其中每一项都是 σ^a，所以乘了 a 次，就是 σ^{a^2}。大家知道，若将 σ^a 自乘 a 次，那就是 σ^{a^2}。
That would give you this, as you kept cancelling out the \tau and \tau^{-1}, and then each one of these is \sigma^a, so you get it a times, so that's \sigma^{a^2}. When you know, if you take \sigma^a, a times, that's \sigma^{a^2}.

117
00:32:43,322 --> 00:32:47,780
另一方面，τ^2 是单位元，所以这也等于σ。
On the other hand, \tau^2 is the identity, so this is \sigma.

118
00:32:52,529 --> 00:32:59,690
一旦将 τ 平方，它就与 σ 对易，所以 σ^{a^2} = σ。
Once you square \tau, it commutes with \sigma, so therefore \sigma^{a^2} = \sigma.

119
00:32:59,690 --> 00:33:24,789
这推导出 a^2 同余于 1mod q；而在模 q 下平方等于 1 的元素只有 ±1 mod q，因为如果 q 整除 a^2 - 1，这等于 (a - 1)(a + 1)；而如果素数整除两个数的乘积，它必须整除其中一个。
So that implies that a^2 is congruent to 1 mod q; and the only elements whose square is 1 mod q are \pm 1 mod q, because if q divides a^2 - 1, this is (a - 1)(a + 1); and if you have a prime that divides a product of numbers, it has to divide one of them.

120
00:33:24,789 --> 00:33:33,142
所以要么 a ≡ 1 mod q，要么 a ≡ -1 mod q。所以这里仅有的可能……这个 a 绝不是任意的！
So either a \equiv 1 mod q, or a \equiv -1 mod q. So the only possibilities here... this a is not arbitrary!

121
00:33:33,142 --> 00:33:47,425
千万不要以为这个 a 可以随便选：它与 τ 的阶密切相关。事实上，我们在那边证明的结论是：a^p 必须模 q 同余于 1。
Don't ever think this a is arbitrary: it's related to the order of \tau. And in fact, what we proved here, over there, what we proved is that a^p has to be congruent to 1 mod q.

122
00:33:47,425 --> 00:34:00,006
因为应用 τ 时——你不该取 τ 的平方，而是取 τ 的 p 次幂，你已知它是单位元。
Because you would apply \tau—you wouldn't take the square of \tau, you take the p-th power of \tau, which you know is the identity.

123
00:34:00,006 --> 00:34:08,042
所以这个实为模 q 整数的 a，必须具有这样的性质：取其 p 次幂后模 q 得到 1。
So this a, which is really a number mod q, has to have the property that when you take its p-th power, you get 1 mod q.

124
00:34:08,042 --> 00:34:22,635
这是模 q 的一个数，因为你只需知道将 σ 升至几次方即可，它在模 q 下不能任意选取：它的 p 次方必须等于 1。所以这里我们看到 a 的平方必须等于 1。
This is a number mod q, because you just have to know what it is to raise \sigma to, and it can't be arbitrary mod q: it has to have its p-th power being 1. So here we see that a has to have its square 1.

125
00:34:22,635 --> 00:34:28,500
模 q 下平方等于 1 的仅有两个元素是 ±1，所以我们只有两种可能：σ 或 σ^{-1}。
The only two elements mod q whose square is 1 are \pm 1, so we have two possibilities: \sigma or \sigma^{-1}.

126
00:34:28,500 --> 00:34:54,480
就像刚才的情况一样：若是 σ，说明 τ 与 σ 对易，群 G 同构于由 τ和 σ 生成的 2q 阶循环群；若是 σ^{-1}，G 则同构于 2q 阶二面体群，因为它包含 q 阶循环子群，
Just like it was here: if it's \sigma, that says \tau commutes with \sigma, and the group G is isomorphic to the cyclic group of order 2q generated by \tau and \sigma; and if it's \sigma^{-1}, G is isomorphic to the dihedral group of order 2q, because it has a cyclic

127
00:34:54,480 --> 00:35:09,685
且含有一个2 阶元素将生成元共轭为其逆元。因此，6 阶群的这个结论对于阶为2q 的群同样成立：要么是循环群，要么是二面体群，非常简单！
subgroup of order q and it has an element of order 2, and that element conjugates the generator into its inverse. So again, this thing of order 6, it's true for groups of order 2q: it's either cyclic or dihedral, very simple!

128
00:35:09,685 --> 00:35:32,603
好，现在我们换掉 2，来试试 3。我们来试试 15 阶。好，现在我们来做这个论证，我迅速给大家解决掉。
Okay, now let's get rid of 2 and try 3. Let's try order 15. Okay, now we're going to do this argument, and I'll kill it for you.

129
00:35:32,603 --> 00:35:54,070
首先，我们有这个由 σ生成的 5 阶正规子群；现在我们还有一个子群 H_3 = {1, τ, τ^2}。虽然我后面用不着，但我顺便向大家证明这个子群也是正规的。
First of all, we have this normal subgroup of order 5 generated by \sigma, and now we have a subgroup H_3 which is {1, \tau, \tau^2}. Now, I'm not going to need this, but I'm also going to show you that this subgroup is normal.

130
00:35:54,070 --> 00:36:09,960
我不需要用到它，但事实上在这种情况下 H_3 实际上也是G 的正规子群；两个西罗子群都是正规的。
I'm not going to need it, but in fact in this case H_3 is actually a normal subgroup of G too; both Sylows are normal.

131
00:36:09,960 --> 00:36:20,892
此前的情形并不必然如此：例如 2 阶元素在对称群中并不构成正规子群，我们已经见过多次了。
That's not necessarily the case here: for example, the elements of order 2 do not form normal subgroups in a symmetric group, we've seen that many times.

132
00:36:20,892 --> 00:36:28,660
好，为什么它正规？因为西罗 3-子群的数目整除 5，对吧，且模 3 同余于 1。
Okay, why is it normal? Because the number of Sylow 3-subgroups divides 5, right, and is congruent to 1 mod 3.

133
00:36:28,660 --> 00:36:44,588
除了 1 以外不存在这样的数：因为西罗 3-子群的数目 ℓ 整除 5 且 ℓ ≡ 1 mod 3。
There are... so There are no such numbers except for 1, as the number \ell of Sylow 3-subgroups divides 5 and is congruent to 1 mod 3.

134
00:36:44,588 --> 00:36:56,725
现在并不是说这不可行……大家知道，3 小于 5，所以模 3 同余于 1 的数原本有可能整除 5，但实际上没有，对吧？
Now it's not the case that this isn't... you know, 3 is smaller than 5, so it's possible that something congruent to 1 mod 3 would divide 5, but nothing does, right?

135
00:36:56,725 --> 00:37:04,420
可能的数是 1、4、7……它们都不能整除 5，所以只能是 1。因此 ℓ = 1，它是正规的。但我们用不着这个。
You get 1, 4, 7... they don't divide 5, so it has to be 1. So \ell = 1, and it's normal. But we won't need that.

136
00:37:04,420 --> 00:37:16,690
直接看这边：我们已知 τ σ τ^{-1} = σ^a，其中 a^3 模5 同余于 1。
Just go over here: we know that \tau \sigma \tau^{-1} = \sigma^a, with a^3 congruent to 1 mod 5.

137
00:37:16,690 --> 00:37:31,952
我断言这推导出 a ≡ 1 mod 5：模 5 下除了 1 以外没有其他 1 的三次根！大家可以直接验算——模 5 的数并不多。
I claim that implies that a is congruent to 1 mod 5: there are no cube roots of 1 mod 5 other than 1! Well, you can just check that—there aren't too many numbers mod 5.

138
00:37:31,952 --> 00:37:49,211
1^3 ≡ 1 mod 5；2^3 = 8，同余于 3 mod 5；3^3 = 27，同余于 2 mod 5；而 4^3 = 64，同余于 4 mod 5。
So: 1^3 is congruent to 1 mod 5; 2^3 is congruent to 8, which is congruent to 3 mod 5; 3^3 is 27, which is congruent to 2 mod 5; and 4^3 is 64, which is congruent to 4 mod 5.

139
00:37:49,211 --> 00:37:53,210
所以模 5 下唯一三次幂等于 1 的数就是 1！
So the only thing mod 5 whose cube is 1 is 1!

140
00:37:53,210 --> 00:38:10,623
这意味着该元素必须等于 σ，从而意味着 τ与 σ 对易，事实上 G 同构于 Z/15Z，由 στ 生成。
Which means that this element has to be equal to \sigma, which means that \tau commutes with \sigma, and in fact that G is isomorphic to Z/15Z, generated by \sigma \tau.

141
00:38:10,623 --> 00:38:29,624
所以这是一个……看起来我们原本以为会得到循环群和非交换群等，但在 15 阶的情形下，恰好只有一种群，而且它是循环群，因为你无法非平凡地解这个方程。
So this is a case... It looked like we were getting, you know, both cyclic groups and non-abelian groups and things, but in the case of order 15, there's only one group, and it's cyclic, because you can't solve this equation in a non-trivial way.

142
00:38:29,624 --> 00:38:56,970
好，我们来看另一个群：G 的阶等于 21，即 3 * 7。在此情形下，H_7 是正规的，但 H_3 可能不正规：
Okay, let's go to another group: order of G is equal to 21, which is 3 * 7. Now in this case, H_7 is normal, but H_3 may not be normal:

143
00:38:56,970 --> 00:39:15,175
在分析出具体群之前我们并不确定。但大家看，上面的论证不适用了，因为可能存在——我们尚不知晓——7 个西罗3-子群，对吧？
we don't know one way or another until we work out the groups. But you see, this argument doesn't work, because there might be—we don't know—be 7 Sylow 3-subgroups, right?

144
00:39:15,175 --> 00:39:28,838
因为西罗 3-子群的数目整除 7 且同余于 1 mod 3。所以可能有 1 个，也可能有7 个：1 个西罗 3-子群，或者 7 个。
Because the number of Sylow 3-subgroups divides 7 and is congruent to 1 mod 3. So there could be 1, or there could be 7: one Sylow 3, or there could be 7.

145
00:39:28,838 --> 00:39:48,515
同样，在此情形下我们得到了非平凡解：如果我们寻找满足 a^3 ≡ 1 mod 7 的解，我们发现 a 可以是 1（1 总是可行），但 2 也可行，而且 4 也可行（mod 7）！
And likewise, in this case we get a non-trivial solution: if we look for a^3 congruent to 1 mod 7, we find that a could be 1—always 1 works—but also 2 works, and also 4 works mod 7!

146
00:39:48,515 --> 00:39:55,511
因为2 的立方是 8，模 7 余 1；4 的立方是 64，等于 63 + 1。
Because if you cube 2 you get 8, which leaves a remainder of 1; and if you cube 4 you get 64, which is 63 + 1.

147
00:39:55,511 --> 00:40:12,150
所以看起来我们有三种可能：我们有 τ σ τ^{-1} = σ，这意味着 τ σ = σ τ，交换群，而且事实证明它同构于 Z/21Z，
So it looks like we have three possibilities: so we have \tau \sigma \tau^{-1} = \sigma, that means that \tau \sigma = \sigma \tau, commutative group, and it turns out that that's isomorphic to Z/21Z,

148
00:40:12,150 --> 00:40:26,445
即 21 阶循环群；我们可以得到 τ σ τ^{-1} = σ^2；或者得到 τ σ τ^{-1}等于 σ^4。
cyclic group of order 21; we could get \tau \sigma \tau^{-1} = \sigma^2; or we could get \tau \sigma \tau^{-1} equal to \sigma^4.

149
00:40:26,445 --> 00:40:46,246
看起来我们又得到了另外两个 21 阶群，但其实不然：这两个给出相同的群，给出同构的21 阶非交换群，含有 7 个西罗 3-子群—
And it looks like we're getting two other groups of order 21, but we're not: these two give the same group, give isomorphic non-abelian groups of order 21 with seven Sylow 3-subgroups—

150
00:40:46,246 --> 00:40:57,678
—抱歉挡着大家了——同构的群。所以 21 阶群只有两种：一种对应 a = 1，而这两组关系给出同一个群。
sorry about that—isomorphic groups. So you get two groups of order 21: the one where it's equal to 1, and these two give the same group.

151
00:40:57,678 --> 00:41:12,785
为什么它们给出同一个群呢？假设我构造了一个具有这个乘法关系的群：τ 是什么？τ 只是这里的元素之一，对吧？
And why do they give the same group? Well, suppose I made a group where I had this multiplicative relation: now what's \tau? Well, \tau is just one of the elements in here, right?

152
00:41:12,785 --> 00:41:34,912
如果我为 H_3 选择另一个生成元，即 τ^2，且 τ 具有把 σ 共轭为 σ^2 的性质，那么 τ^2 就具有把 σ 共轭为 σ^4 的性质！而在这个群中，τ 与 τ^2 并没有哪个更优越。
If I chose the other generator for H_3, that's \tau^2, and \tau had the property of conjugating \sigma into \sigma^2, then \tau^2 would have the property of conjugating \sigma into \sigma^4! And in this group there's no preferred \tau or \tau^2.

153
00:41:34,912 --> 00:41:54,299
所以如果我有一个包含 σ 和 τ 的群满足前一个关系，我就可以建立一个与另一个群的同构（通过将 τ 映为 τ^2），满足后一个关系，因此它们是同构的群。所以并不是说不同的 a 值总是给出不同的群。
So if I had a group with \sigma and \tau that did this, I could make an isomorphism with another group by sending \tau to \tau^2 that did this, and they are isomorphic groups. So it's not that sometimes different values of a give you a new group.

154
00:41:54,299 --> 00:42:07,569
a = 1 总是给出循环群，我应该写下来：a = 1 给出 G 同构于 Z/pqZ，由 στ 生成。
a = 1 always gives the cyclic group, I should write that down: a = 1 gives G isomorphic to Z/pqZ, generated by \sigma \tau.

155
00:42:07,569 --> 00:42:25,470
我们总是知道这一种：总存在一种 pq 阶群，即循环群；在某些情况下（如 15），我们只能得到这一种；而在其他情况下（如 2q），我们得到两种群；在此处我们得到两种群。也可能得到更多种！可以得到更多。
We always know that one: there's always one group of order pq, the cyclic group; and in some cases, like 15, we only get that; in other cases, like 2q, we get two groups; here we get two groups. You can get more! You can get more.

156
00:42:25,470 --> 00:42:34,173
好，现在书上有一个极佳的练习（我先带大家起个头），展示了这个问题是如何迅速变得复杂的。
Okay, now the book does a great exercise, which I'm going to start for you, where they show you how this quickly becomes more complicated.

157
00:42:34,173 --> 00:42:42,351
所以我们真的……我们对自己能分类 pq 阶群感到相当自豪了。我们这里有相当一般性的理论，可以在任何具体情况下求解。
So we're really... we're getting pretty proud of ourselves doing the groups of order pq. We have a pretty general theory over here, we can work it out in any given case.

158
00:42:42,351 --> 00:42:51,253
但假设我们把难度稍微提高一点，探讨类似 p^2 * q 这种阶数的群呢？
But suppose we jazz it up just a little bit, and we ask for the groups of order something like p^2 * q?

159
00:42:51,253 --> 00:43:07,770
例如，书上有很棒的一小节（我建议大家仔细读读，我先带大家开个头），专门讨论 12 阶群，即 2^2 * 3。
For example, the book does a nice section, which I suggest you go through, and I'll start with you, on the groups of order 12, which is 2^2 * 3.

160
00:43:07,770 --> 00:43:18,683
在这里情况变得有趣得多了。事实证明……好的，谢谢，谢谢。
Now here things get much more interesting. It turns out... yeah, no, thank you, thank you.

161
00:43:18,683 --> 00:43:29,969
你实际上……那么还不能完全确定，你必须证明这类关系不会引出进一步的矛盾；有一种用生成元与关系给出群的方法。
You actually... then it's it's not clear, you have to show that this kind of relation doesn't lead you into further contradiction; and there's a method of presenting groups.

162
00:43:29,969 --> 00:43:49,698
所以这个群可以这样给出：我会说取群 G 由 σ 和 τ 生成，满足 σ^7 = e，τ^3 = e，以及 τ σ τ^{-1} = σ^2。
So this group would be presented: I would say take the group G generated by \sigma and \tau such that \sigma^7 is the identity, \tau^3 is the identity, and \tau \sigma \tau^{-1} = \sigma^2.

163
00:43:49,698 --> 00:43:51,465
我会说：“这就是那个 21 阶群”。
I'd say, "There's your group of order 21."

164
00:43:51,465 --> 00:44:03,035
而你会说：“非常好，你现在告诉我如何对调 τ 和 σ 了，我知道群里的元素是 σ 的幂乘 τ 的幂，但是……我会不会因此遇到麻烦？
And you'd say, "That's very nice, you know, you've now told me how to commute \tau and \sigma, I know the group is powers of \sigma and powers of \tau, but am I going to get into trouble with that?

165
00:44:03,035 --> 00:44:16,161
后面会不会出现某种矛盾，比如某个元素的某次幂既等于单位元又同时不等于单位元？”所以你必须有办法证明这样的群确实存在。我们曾通过几何构造知道了二面体群的存在。
Is there some contradiction that's going to come up later, where I have some power of some element is equal to the identity, but not equal to the identity?" And you have to have a way of then proving this group exists. We knew about the dihedral group from geometric construction.

166
00:44:16,161 --> 00:44:28,049
要证明该群存在：这被称为——在后面章节会讲——考克斯特展示（Coxeter presentation），以一位加拿大伟大数学家命名，他刚去世不久，享年 97 岁，
So to prove this group exists: this is called—and it's later in the chapter—a Coxeter presentation, after a great Canadian mathematician who just died in fact at the age of 97, H.S.M. Coxeter.

167
00:44:28,049 --> 00:44:41,099
即 H. S. M. 考克斯特。你必须切实证明可以用这些生成元和关系构造出一个群。这并非显而易见，但在此我们至少可以看出，除了循环群之外至多只有一个群。
And you have to actually show that you can construct a group with these generators and relations. That's not obvious, but all we can see here is that there's at most one more group beyond the cyclic group.

168
00:44:41,099 --> 00:45:10,996
好，12 阶群：事实上有 5 个互不同构的群，其中两个是交换群，两个是交换群：一个是 Z/12Z，另一个是直积 Z/6Z × Z/2Z，两个群的直积。
All right, the groups of order 12: turns out that there are five distinct groups, of which two are abelian, two are abelian: so one of them is Z/12Z, another one is Z/6Z \times Z/2Z, product of two groups.

169
00:45:10,996 --> 00:45:18,940
它们不是同一个群，因为前一个群只有 1 个 2 阶元素，而后一个群有 3 个 2 阶元素。
These aren't the same group, because this group has only one element of order 2 in it, whereas this group has 3 elements of order 2 in it.

170
00:45:18,940 --> 00:45:34,734
一个是 4 个字母上的交错群 A_4，一个是 12 阶二面体群 D_{12}，还有一个是你们以前从未见过的全新群。
One is the alternating group on 4 letters A_4, one is the dihedral group of order 12 D_{12}, and one is something new that you haven't seen before.

171
00:45:34,734 --> 00:45:45,862
我们正是通过相同的分类方法来找出这些群的，只不过步骤要复杂得多。那么为什么会变得更复杂呢？
And we uncover these groups by going through the same kind of classification, except that it becomes much more complicated. So why does it become more complicated?

172
00:45:45,862 --> 00:45:57,397
从西罗定理中我们得到：在 G 中存在一个 4 阶子群 H_4，以及一个 3 阶子群 H_3。
Well, what we get from the Sylow theorem is: we have a subgroup H_4 in G of order 4, and we have a subgroup H_3 in G of order 3.

173
00:45:57,397 --> 00:46:19,783
对于 H_3，我们知道它是循环群，因为它的阶是素数；但对于 H_4，我们只知道它是交换群，因为它的阶是 p^2。所以它要么同构于 Z/4Z，要么同构于 (Z/2Z)^2。
So this group we know is a cyclic group, because it has prime order; but this group we just know is an abelian group, because it has order p^2. So this can be either isomorphic to Z/4Z, or to (Z/2Z)^2.

174
00:46:20,714 --> 00:46:40,803
所以这里已经出现了一种不确定性，即我们不知道西罗 2-子群的具体结构：我们只知道有 4 阶子群，而不知道其结构……我们确实知道西罗 3-子群的结构。在 pq 阶的情形中，较大阶数的子群总是正规子群。
So already we have an ambiguity, in that we don't know what the structure is of the Sylow 2-subgroup: we just know there's something of order 4, and we don't know what the structure... We do know what the structure of the Sylow 3-subgroup is. Now in the pq case, the larger one was always a normal subgroup.

175
00:46:40,803 --> 00:46:47,211
好，但我断言在此例中，两者都不必然……两者都不一定必须是正规的。
Okay, so I claim that in this case, neither of them have... you know, neither of them has to be normal.

176
00:46:47,211 --> 00:47:04,640
让我们看看西罗定理关于我们有多少个西罗 2-子群以及多少个西罗 3-子群是怎么说的。西罗 2-子群的数目必须整除 3，对吧，且模 2 同余于 1。
So let's see what the Sylow theorems tell us about the question of how many Sylow 2's we have, and how many Sylow 3's we have. Well, the number of Sylow 2-subgroups has to divide 3, right, and be congruent to 1 mod 2.

177
00:47:04,640 --> 00:47:15,560
有哪些可能？3 的因子中模 2 同余于 1 的有哪些？正是如此！
So what are the possibilities? What are the divisors of 3 which are congruent to 1 mod 2? There we go!

178
00:47:15,560 --> 00:47:26,063
好，否则我讲得太快了。所以西罗 2-子群的数目 ℓ 等于 1 或 3。
Okay, otherwise I was going much too fast. So the number \ell of Sylow 2-subgroups is equal to 1 or 3.

179
00:47:26,063 --> 00:47:54,146
西罗 3-子群的数目 ℓ 必须整除 4，且必须模 3 同余于 1：1 或 4！很好！所以特别地，两者都不一定必须正规，但我断言两者中至少有一个是正规的！
The number \ell of Sylow 3-subgroups has to divide 4, and has to be congruent to 1 mod 3: 1 or 4! Good! So in particular, neither of them has to be normal, but I claim one or the other is normal!

180
00:47:54,146 --> 00:48:04,802
也就是说，你不可能同时拥有 3 个西罗 2-子群和 4 个西罗 3-子群。绝不可能，这根本不会发生。
Namely, you can't have 3 Sylow 2's and 4 Sylow 3's. You can't have it, it just won't happen.

181
00:48:04,802 --> 00:48:25,232
为什么？假设我们有 4 个西罗 3-子群。好的，这是群的示意图：这是 G，这是单位元，这里是一个西罗 3-子群。
Why? Well, imagine we had four Sylow 3-subgroups. Okay, here's the picture of the group: here's G, here's the identity element, and here's a Sylow 3-subgroup.

182
00:48:25,232 --> 00:48:29,931
它包含两个非平凡元素，对吧，σ 和 σ^2，我们有 4 个这样的子群。
It has two non-trivial elements in it, right, \sigma and \sigma^2, and we have four of those.

183
00:48:29,931 --> 00:48:39,083
我断言它们两两不相交：这些群唯一的交集是单位元，因为它们的阶是素数。
Now I claim they're all distinct: the only intersection of those groups is the identity, because their order is prime.

184
00:48:39,083 --> 00:48:45,465
两个素数阶群的交集要么是同一个群，要么只有平凡单位元。
So if you have an intersection of two groups of prime order, they either have to be the same group, or their intersection is trivial.

185
00:48:45,465 --> 00:48:53,250
所以在每一个这样的子群中，我都得到两个 3 阶元素，于是这给我提供了 8 个 3 阶元素。
So in each one of these, I get two elements of order 3, so that gives me 8 elements of order 3.

186
00:48:54,550 --> 00:49:09,830
此外还有一个 1 阶元素（单位元），所以群里只剩下 3 个尚未计入、阶不为 1 或 3 的元素！
And also I have one element of order 1, so there are only three elements left in this group that haven't been accounted for, that don't have order 1 or 3!

187
00:49:09,830 --> 00:49:17,417
现在，一个 4 阶的西罗 2-子群恰好包含 3 个非单位元。
Now, a Sylow 2-subgroup of order 4 contains three non-identity elements.

188
00:49:17,417 --> 00:49:35,390
所以唯一的可能就是：如果有 4 个西罗 3-子群，单位元加上这3 个元素必须构成那个 4 阶西罗子群，因为出于整除性原因，4 阶西罗子群与西罗 3-子群不能有非平凡交集。
So the only possibility is: if I had four Sylow 3-subgroups, the identity plus these three elements must be the Sylow 4-subgroup, because the Sylow 4 cannot have any non-trivial intersection with the Sylow 3's, for divisibility reasons again.

189
00:49:35,390 --> 00:49:48,599
因此单位元 e与剩下的 3 个元素的并集必须是 4 阶西罗 2-子群；这意味着西罗 4 阶子群不可能再有其他可能，对吧？
So then e union the three remaining elements has to be a Sylow 2-subgroup of order 4, which means there are no other possibilities for Sylow 4-subgroups, right?

190
00:49:48,599 --> 00:50:01,619
因为它们全都是共轭的，而我已经找出了它的全部元素，这意味着该 4 阶西罗子群是正规的！所以若有 4 个西罗 3-子群，就只能有 1 个西罗 2-子群！所以 4 推导出 1。
Because they all have to be conjugate, and I've just told you what it is, which means the Sylow 4 is normal! So if we have four Sylow 3's, we only have one Sylow 2! So this 4 implies 1.

191
00:50:01,619 --> 00:50:16,145
因此至少有一个子群是正规的：它们可能都正规，例如在 12 阶循环群中，或者在这个群中两者都是正规子群，但至少有一个是正规的。
So therefore at least something is normal: they might both be normal, like in the cyclic group of order 12, or in this group they're both normal subgroups, but at least one of them is normal.

192
00:50:16,145 --> 00:50:27,955
好，接下来的推导就基于至少有一个是正规的这一事实，并且我们已知这些子群的结构，从而导出全部 5 种可能。我是说，你从这里入手：好的，假设西罗 2-子群正规，我们能从中得到什么？
Okay, so the proof then proceeds from the fact that at least one is normal, and that we know the structure of these groups, to derive the five possibilities. I mean, you start off with: okay, let's assume the Sylow 2 is normal, what can we get from that?

193
00:50:27,955 --> 00:50:47,939
好的，假设西罗 3-子群正规……顺便提一句，这是西罗 2-子群正规的情形，而这是西罗 3-子群正规而另一个不正规的情形，所以两种路径都可以走。
Okay, let's assume the Sylow 3 is normal. This is a case, by the way, where the Sylow 2 is normal, and this is a case, by the way, where the Sylow 3 is normal, but not the other one. So you can go both ways.

194
00:50:47,939 --> 00:50:58,530
因此我强烈建议大家：为了练习西罗定理是如何运作的、以及如何从群的内部信息拼装出一个群，大家去完整走一遍这个12 阶群的分类。
So I strongly suggest, just to practice working out how the Sylow theorems work, how you put together a group from its inside information, you go through this classification of groups of order 12.

195
00:50:58,530 --> 00:51:03,858
这并不是世界上最重要的事，只是检验大家是否掌握了这些技巧的一种方式。
It's not the most important thing in the world, it's just a way of testing that you understand the techniques.

196
00:51:03,858 --> 00:51:13,422
正如你们可以想象的，阶数增加时情况会越来越复杂：如果不考虑 12 阶群而是 24 阶群，西罗 2-子群的阶为 8，
And as you can imagine, this gets more and more complicated: if instead of the group of order 12, it's for the group of order 24, so the Sylow 2-subgroup has order 8,

197
00:51:13,422 --> 00:51:28,666
那么8 阶群本身就已经有 5 种可能作为西罗 2-子群，更不用说西罗 3-子群如何作用在它上面了！所以这种分类会变成一场不折不扣的噩梦。
there are already there are already five possibilities for that group of order 8 that could be the Sylow 2, let alone how the Sylow 3 is acting on it! So the classification becomes quite, quite a nightmare.

198
00:51:28,666 --> 00:51:31,953
尽管如此，这正是有限群理论学家们最爱做的事情！
Nonetheless, this is the sort of thing finite group theorists love to do!

199
00:51:31,953 --> 00:51:43,322
所以下次我来上课时，我会把《有限单群图集》（Atlas）带过来，让大家看看他们做出的所有精彩成就；理查德周五将开始讲对称群。
So next time I'm in, I'll bring in the *Atlas*, so you can see all the wonderful things they've done; and Richard will start on Friday with the symmetric group.
